{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And a man.</b> To exclude a minor." "<b>Who lies with another man's wife.</b> To exclude the wife of a minor — this teaches us that a minor has no betrothal. And which married woman have I obligated to you?" "<b>Who lies with his fellow's wife.</b> To exclude the wife of a gentile — this teaches us that there is no betrothal for a gentile (Sifra; Sanhedrin 52)." "<b>They shall surely be put to death, the adulterer and the adulteress.</b> Every death-penalty stated in the Torah without specification is nothing but strangulation (Sifra; Sanhedrin 55)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:24.365359185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}